WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.239 line:16% position:4% align:start
Getting dressed is one of those everyday tasks that

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:05.679 line:16% position:4% align:start
still sends you back and forth between a closet,

00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:08.118 line:16% position:4% align:start
a mirror, and a weather app. Aura puts the

00:00:08.118 --> 00:00:10.558 line:16% position:4% align:start
mirror first and brings the controls in when you

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:11.100 line:16% position:4% align:start
need them.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.103 line:16% position:4% align:start
Aura starts as a mirror with a compact assistant

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:18.306 line:16% position:4% align:start
in the upper corner. The wardrobe stays out of

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:21.509 line:16% position:4% align:start
the way. This recording uses a public test image

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:24.000 line:16% position:4% align:start
for the camera and simulated speech transcripts.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.756 line:16% position:4% align:start
Good evening, sir. Welcome home. In San Francisco, it's

00:00:30.756 --> 00:00:33.149 line:16% position:4% align:start
60 degrees Fahrenheit and overcast.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.839 line:16% position:4% align:start
Asking to try on some clothes brings up the

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:50.279 line:16% position:4% align:start
closet. It has real photographs of tees, a polo,

00:00:50.279 --> 00:00:52.189 line:16% position:4% align:start
a denim jacket and jeans.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.200 line:16% position:4% align:start
The new shirt appears over the detected garment. A

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.100 line:16% position:4% align:start
worker updates the clothing mask and shoulders. A lightweight

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.000 line:16% position:4% align:start
tracker moves the fabric between updates. The live image

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.167 line:16% position:4% align:start
processing runs on this computer.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.150 line:16% position:4% align:start
Changing shirts uses the same camera view, so you

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.171 line:16% position:4% align:start
can compare colors and graphics on the spot.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.385 line:16% position:4% align:start
The preview follows the shape of the visible torso.

00:01:28.385 --> 00:01:31.671 line:16% position:4% align:start
It gives an impression of the fabric and color.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.696 line:16% position:4% align:start
Jackets use the upper-body preview too. Jeans are available

00:01:38.696 --> 00:01:40.943 line:16% position:4% align:start
through the separate photo mode.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.401 line:16% position:4% align:start
To try something from your wardrobe, hold it up

00:01:46.401 --> 00:01:49.352 line:16% position:4% align:start
to the camera or upload a photo. You can

00:01:49.352 --> 00:01:52.303 line:16% position:4% align:start
try it immediately or save it for another day.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:03.189 line:16% position:4% align:start
When you ask for suggestions, Meta Muse Spark looks

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.529 line:16% position:4% align:start
at the garment photo and fills in its name,

00:02:06.529 --> 00:02:09.868 line:16% position:4% align:start
category, and color. You can edit these details before

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:10.239 line:16% position:4% align:start
saving.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.183 line:16% position:4% align:start
Aura keeps the continuous video and wardrobe on the

00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:23.115 line:16% position:4% align:start
device. Meta vision is used for the still image

00:02:23.115 --> 00:02:27.048 line:16% position:4% align:start
requests you initiate. The repository includes a Raspberry Pi

00:02:27.048 --> 00:02:27.922 line:16% position:4% align:start
camera adapter.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.049 line:16% position:4% align:start
Aura Mirror is open source. Thanks for watching.
